         <div type="translation" xml:lang="en">
            <ab xml:lang=" en">
               <pb n="" />
               <lb n="x+1 " />They have spoken [///] <lb n="x+2 " />One is used to quarrel with him <lb n="x+3 " />concerning a matter. Petemous does not belong <lb n="x+4 " />to those people whose <lb n="x+5 " />hands (can) be taken in a matter. There is <lb n="x+6 " />a letter made by the wab priests <supplied reason="lost">of … </supplied>
               <lb n="x+7 " />to the <supplied reason="omitted">of … </supplied>. One knows <lb n="x+8 " />the strong one, who arose(?). I could not <lb n="x+9 " /><supplied cert="high" reason="omitted">cause </supplied>a wab priest to come to the south. <lb n="x+10 " />The wab priests of Osiris who are (also) priests of Chnoum <lb n="x+11 " />and who (live) here, inquired about him. <lb n="x+12 " />They agreed. They wrote a letter <lb n="x+13 " />to the wab priests, too. <lb n="x+14 " />The lesonis <lb n="x+15 " />may be ordered to cause me <lb n="x+16 " />to hear about the suspension <lb n="x+17 " />which is to be granted to Petemous <lb n="x+18 " />because of Peteesis, his son. And it should be caused, that <lb n="x+19 " />Petemous send to me concerning everything <lb n="x+20 " />which shall be done to him. If it happens <lb n="x+21 " />that here is something (which is desired): One may order <lb n="x+22 " />to cause to send to me concerning it! Written by <lb n="x+23 "
                   />Teonurisephonychos, son of Imouthes, in <lb n="x+24 " />the 9th regnal year, 4th of Payni. </ab>
         </div>
